\\sqrt{3})$ is defined\n- **III.** ${f}_{y}(0,1)$ is defined" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186409557 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0a3b6388-98bd-5083-8d1c-f60a05890b23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409557 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{x}{y})}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}+1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{x}{y})}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}+1}\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(\\sqrt{3},1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(\\sqrt{3},1)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{1})=\\frac{\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\nand both partial derivatives are also defined at $(\\sqrt{3},1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(\\sqrt{3},1) & =\\frac{1}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{1}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {f}_{y}(\\sqrt{3},1) & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{1}^{2}}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the function $f$ itself is defined at $(1,\\sqrt{3})$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,\\sqrt{3})=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{x}$ is also defined at $(1,\\sqrt{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is also true. Indeed, the function $f$ itself is defined at $(0,1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(0,1)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{0}{1})=0,\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(0,1)=-\\frac{0}{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409560 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409560 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "06a4b700-aa67-595f-ad77-c3a9c2d08fa3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409560 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409561 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409561 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1786d23c-6b2b-5b25-8a34-a3df54af58bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409561 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186339043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409562 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409562 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "488b6ab6-cae5-5979-9b52-c3723c3f093b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409562 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186335822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409563 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409563 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "61817e36-5704-54ae-b054-a7bf550b56c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409563 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409564 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "be87cbb6-8a21-5895-a193-08d9d1a311c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409564 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426702 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426702 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426702 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426702 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426702 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426702 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426702 #edb/ref 1045 "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions" #edb/ref 1759218